  "scenario_narratives": {
    "base": "Indicor Instrumentation (~$1.1bn sales, recurring consumables/aftermarket) is folded into EIG and EMG on AMETEK's usual Operational Excellence playbook; the record $4.1bn backlog and +25% organic orders support ~6% organic growth next year fading to ~3-4% as aerospace/defense and process-instrument cycles normalise. Tariff costs (~$70m in 2025) continue to be priced through. Blended EBITDA margin dips on Indicor in year 1 then recovers ~1pp. Free cash flow goes to deleveraging from ~2.3x rather than buybacks or new deals; no further acquisitions are credited.",
    "bull": "The order surge (+28%, EMG +35% organic) proves to be the front end of a multi-year aerospace, defense and automation upcycle, sustaining 7-9% organic growth for several years; AMETEK lifts Indicor's margins to group level as it has with prior deals, pushing pre-SBC EBITDA margin toward 34%. The market continues to pay a premium multiple for a compounder with this record (20x terminal cap).",
    "bear": "The 2026 order spike is pre-tariff pull-forward and aerospace restocking that reverses: organic sales fall ~1% next year and grow only 2-3% after, as China exposure and trade policy weigh on process and analytical instruments. Indicor, AMETEK's largest-ever deal, integrates poorly and dilutes margins; with leverage at ~2.3x the compounding M&A engine stalls. Margins give back ~2pp to ~30% and the market re-rates the name to an industrial multiple (15x cap, 2.5% terminal growth)."
  },
  "valuation_philosophy": {
    "summary": "AMETEK is valued as a mature, high-margin niche-instrument compounder on an owner-FCF basis, using organic growth only: the acquisition half of its historical growth algorithm is not credited, because the FCF that would fund future deals is already counted as distributable. Indicor is included from its closing (revenue and the ~$5bn of debt that paid for it).",
    "key_risks_to_valuation": [
      "Indicor integration: ~$5bn, the largest deal in AMETEK's history, closed 26-Aug-2026; its margin and growth are assumed, not yet reported",
      "Pro forma net debt is an estimate (June balance sheet + ~$5bn deal debt); the Q3 10-Q will fix it",
      "Order surge may be pull-forward ahead of tariffs or aerospace restocking",
      "Terminal value is roughly three-quarters of EV; the 18x cap binds in the base case",
      "Excluding future M&A is conservative relative to how the market values AMETEK's capital-deployment record"
    ]
  },
