    "notes": "MODEL: owner-FCF component DCF (routing: US diversified industrial operating company; no bank/REIT/holdco features). First valuation of AME. BASE PERIOD: TTM to 30 Jun 2026 rather than FY2025 so that H1-2026 cash flow (already reflected in the June balance sheet via debt paydown) is not counted twice. NET DEBT: June 2026 debt 2,036 - cash 495 = 1,541, plus ~5,000 of new borrowing for the all-cash Indicor Instrumentation acquisition (closed 26-Aug-2026) = 6,541 pro forma; cross-check: mgmt's ~2.3x leverage at close on ~2.84bn pro forma EBITDA ~ 6.5bn. Q3 operating cash between July and close ignored (conservative). FY2025 XBRL TotalDebt (3,492) looks inflated relative to adjacent quarters and was not used. REVENUE: year 1 (Jul-26..Jun-27) = TTM x ~1.06 organic + ~10 months of Indicor (~$1.1bn/yr -> ~$0.92bn) = +17.7%; year 2 adds the last 2 months of Indicor plus ~5% organic. Beyond that growth is ORGANIC ONLY: AMETEK's historical 8-10% revenue CAGR is part-acquired with FCF, and owner FCF here is treated as fully distributable, so compounding acquired growth on top would count the reinvested cash twice. EBITDA margin is pre-SBC (XBRL EBITDA = operating income + D&A, which is post-SBC; TTM 31.2% + SBC 0.6% = 31.9%); Indicor assumed ~30% EBITDA margin, diluting the blend slightly in year 1. D&A includes large acquired-intangible amortisation (~5.3% of revenue TTM, higher post-Indicor) and glides to ~capex+ by year 10 so the amortisation tax shield is not perpetuated. Working capital: manufacturer, capture -10% of revenue change (slightly over-charges year 1 because Indicor's working capital was bought with the purchase price). BUYBACKS: AMETEK is a repurchaser (FY2025 $434m, H1-26 $28m) so the flat count is funded, though repurchases will pause while Indicor debt is paid down.",
